# Copy to .dev.vars for local development.

# GITHUB_TOKEN is required for almost everything: there are no fixtures
# left in this codebase (see docs/decisions/ADR-002-mcp-vs-direct-tools.md)
# — PR/CI data, the open-PR list, and merge/close all call the real
# GitHub API for GITHUB_REPO. Without it, those all degrade to
# null/empty/no-op rather than throwing, but the demo has nothing real to
# show. A fine-grained PAT scoped to just GITHUB_REPO with read-only
# Contents + Pull requests covers everything except merge/close, which
# additionally need Pull requests: Read and write.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...
# GITHUB_REPO is the repo PRs are analyzed/merged/closed against —
# deliberately NOT this repo (using ForgeGuard shouldn't mean ForgeGuard
# changing its own source — see ADR-021), defaults to
# "NAVEENKUMARKR777/forgeguard-demo" (set in wrangler.jsonc `vars`).
# GITHUB_REPO=owner/repo

# DEPLOY_REPO is a different thing: it's always the repo actually
# deployed as this Worker (this one), used only by gitops/state.ts to
# compare real git history against the real deployed commit. Doesn't
# track GITHUB_REPO — see ADR-021. Defaults to
# "NAVEENKUMARKR777/forgeguard" (set in wrangler.jsonc `vars`).
# DEPLOY_REPO=owner/repo

# MODEL_PROVIDER defaults to "workers-ai" (set in wrangler.jsonc `vars`) and
# needs `wrangler login` / a Cloudflare account, not a key here. Set it here
# instead — `.dev.vars` overrides wrangler.jsonc's `vars` for local dev, no
# editing wrangler.jsonc needed — to use a different provider:
#
# MODEL_PROVIDER=openai / anthropic — implemented against each provider's
# documented contract but untested in this repo's own development
# environment (no API key was available to test with). See
# docs/decisions/ADR-006-model-providers.md.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
# MODEL_PROVIDER=groq — an OpenAI-compatible REST API, verified end-to-end
# against a real key (see docs/decisions/ADR-019-groq-provider.md). Uses
# openai/gpt-oss-120b (Groq's own recommended replacement for the now
# Groq-deprecated llama-3.3-70b-versatile — Workers AI's own Llama 3.3
# above is unaffected, the deprecation is Groq-side only).
# MODEL_PROVIDER=groq
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...

# Needed for the real GitOps drift check (mcp/cloudflare.ts +
# gitops/state.ts — compares the real deployed Worker version against
# DEPLOY_REPO's master HEAD). A token scoped to Account -> Workers
# Scripts: Read is enough locally; CI's deploy job needs Edit to actually
# deploy. Without these, GitOps drift degrades to "unknown" rather than
# throwing.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=...
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=...
